ok 10 - control: the schedule commits with healthy proof
ok 11 - the schedule wrote exactly one summary row: operation, outcome, blocking count, checker key and version [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 12 - the row is owner-scoped, carries the proof's input hash, is keyed to the exact audit event of the schedule command and has no outbox event (none exists until execution) [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 13 - the schedule resource does not echo the proof's hashes [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 14 - an exact replay writes no second summary row [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 15 - refused schedules (absent, stale, mis-bound or blocked proof, another failed category) write no summary row: the rows roll back with the command [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 16 - the publication wrote exactly one summary row against the lineage row [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 17 - the row references the publication's outbox event and is keyed to the exact audit event of the lineage row [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 18 - an exact replay of the publication writes no second summary row [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 19 - control: a completed, a blocked (publication_not_active), a retried (failed run), an unproven and a failed-category execution, and a stale-proof execution refused with the typed conflict (DEC-158(c))
ok 20 - a verified proof is summarized whether the execution completes, blocks or retries: healthy, healthy, failed and blocked (two findings) [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 21 - absent proof and stale proof are never summarized (nothing was verified) [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 22 - a completed execution's row names the publication event and is keyed to the exact audit event of the lineage row it appended [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 23 - the blocked and retried outcomes (no event) carry no outbox id and each summary is keyed to the exact block or retry audit event of its schedule: four summaries, four distinct audit events [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 24 - a repeated execution (already_completed) writes no further summary row [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 25 - control: two schedule commands reusing one correlation id each wrote their own audit record under it
ok 26 - with a shared correlation id each summary still points at ITS command's audit event: the correlation id alone cannot tell them apart, the audit key can [P2-S11-AC-101]
